---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/attentive-alternative';
const title = "Attentive alternatives: replace the channel, the service, or both?";
const desc = "Plan an Attentive replacement around email and SMS ownership, reply handling, capture permissions and service handover.";
const faqs = [{"question": "Must I replace Attentive email when changing SMS?", "answer": "No. Inventory your actual channels and dependencies, then replace only the accepted scope. Price and test any retained integration."}, {"question": "Will the new sender answer customer replies?", "answer": "Verify the product, region, staffed hours and escalation arrangement. Sending SMS does not establish an agent service or transfer open conversations."}, {"question": "How long should migration take?", "answer": "Set timing from permission reconciliation, sender readiness, queue checks and service acceptance. There is no universal schedule or demonstrated result on this page."}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} dateModified="2026-11-25" />
<main class="container py-16">
<a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a>
<article class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
<h1>{title}</h1>
<p>An Attentive switch can change who answers customers as well as who schedules campaigns. Start with the work your account actually uses. The exercises below are proposed acceptance checks, not performed tests or merchant results.</p>
<h2>Keep Attentive when the operating model fits</h2>
<p>Attentive offers <a href="https://www.attentive.com/email-marketing">email alongside SMS</a>; leaving does not inherently mean adding an email platform. Keep it when your existing capture, channel coordination and support arrangements solve your workload at an acceptable quoted cost. Before replacing it, try repairing a weak journey: remove duplicate entry, clarify approval ownership and inspect purchase exits. Compare the repaired baseline with the replacement proposal.</p>
<h2>Separate platform support from customer replies</h2>
<p>The <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4460351735060-Get-started-with-Attentive-Concierge">Concierge guide</a> describes agents using your service materials to answer subscribers. The <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4405278840852-FAQs-Attentive-Concierge">FAQ</a> positions this as a supplement to your support team. Establish whether you use that product, another helpdesk integration or your own team. Strategy advice, campaign execution and shopper support need separate owners and prices; none follows automatically from buying a channel.</p>
<h2>Choose a replacement path by the missing job</h2>
<p>For a shared ecommerce email/SMS workflow, compare <a href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend</a>: its <a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/2871974-create-your-omnisend-account">account guide</a> documents email, SMS and web push workflows. For a Shopify SMS shortlist, evaluate <a href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> using the same reply and purchase-exit script; retain your current email system if it already works. For behavioral segmentation, investigate <a href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a>. These are procurement paths, not rankings or promises that any candidate replaces your service team.</p>
<h2>Make capture promises portable before changing forms</h2>
<p>Inventory each popup, checkout field, keyword and QR destination, the exact disclosure, channel, source and timestamp recorded, and the journey it starts. A customer who permits email is not thereby eligible for SMS. Rehearse new, existing, declined and previously opted-out contacts on your storefront. Require the new form to retain the evidence you need without re-enrolling a suppressed person or starting two welcome journeys. Save failed cases before replacing the live capture unit.</p>
<h2>Rebuild event authority and waiting messages</h2>
<p>For cart, paid order, cancellation and subscription renewal, write the source event, stable customer/order identifiers, event time and eligible message purpose. Propose fixtures for duplicate delivery, late payment and a purchase while a cart text waits. Inspect dispatch eligibility and both channel queues. Define a maximum acceptable event delay for your operation and stop rollout if the new path cannot meet it; this page does not claim those controls are native or already verified.</p>
<h2>Hand over conversations with an accountable human</h2>
<p>Export the open-case inventory where available, including the last customer question, promised follow-up, owner and unresolved order issue. Minimize personal data to what the receiving team needs. Demonstrate a product question, delivery complaint and escalation outside staffed hours. Concierge documentation distinguishes <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4460366171156-Optimize-messages-for-Concierge">subscriber responses from support and conversational keywords</a>. Recreate those routes deliberately. Require acknowledgement of each open case; a subscriber export does not transfer a conversation queue.</p>
<h2>Approve permission and sender handling separately</h2>
<p>Reconcile opt-outs and permission evidence by channel and purpose. Demonstrate withdrawal after scheduling, an ambiguous reply and a missing timezone; agree which messages pause and who resolves exceptions. Verify sender registration, number portability, reply routing and destination support with both suppliers before announcing a cutover. No universal quiet-hours window or vendor-wide compliance guarantee substitutes for destination-specific review.</p>
<h2>Preserve creative intent without assuming asset transfer</h2>
<p>Keep template purpose, approved offer, expiry, product links, fallback content and brand tone in the handover packet. Rebuild one email and one text with your actual catalog. Check mobile rendering, invalid links, unavailable inventory, encoding and billed segments. Obtain approval for what an agent may offer or promise. A copied template is not proof that dynamic fields, permissions or live offer logic survived.</p>
<h2>Compare economics against the repaired baseline</h2>
<p>Request same-period quotes for actual channel mix, destinations, message segments, profiles, seats, service hours and peak volume. Add retained tools, agent labor, migration and overlap. For a proposed randomized pilot, compare contribution per assigned eligible customer over the same observation window: net sales after discounts and refunds, less goods, fulfillment, messaging and allocated platform/support cost. Do not subtract discounts twice. Platform attribution is not measured causal lift, and service savings count only if the corresponding work is actually removed.</p>
<h2>Cut over only the accepted scope</h2>
<p>Keep unaccepted channels and service work with their existing owner. Reconcile subscriber counts by permission state, sample queued exits and name the person who can stop sends. Record a rollback that restores one sending authority and reconciles new opt-outs before restarting; never simply enable both old and new campaigns. Retain unresolved conversations until the receiving team accepts them. Use the <a href="/apps/attentive">Attentive evaluation</a> for initial product fit and this handover record for the replacement decision.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</main>
</BaseLayout>
